function settingsPage(){return `${head('Workspace settings','Local runtime configuration and data handling.')}<div class="section-grid"><section class="panel"><div class="panel-head"><h2>Local evidence store</h2><span>SQLITE</span></div><div class="settings-box">TraceBack stores imported records in a local SQLite database. The server binds to 127.0.0.1 by default. Imported content is treated as data and escaped in generated reports.<br><br>Upload limit: 10 MB. Supported formats: JSON, JSONL, CSV. PCAP parsing is not enabled in this offline runtime.<br><br>Sample events are synthetic and marked with a source reference. Loading the sample adds missing fixture records without deleting imported evidence.</div></section><section class="panel"><div class="panel-head"><h2>Rule transparency</h2><span>DETERMINISTIC</span></div><div class="settings-box">The TCP port fan-out heuristic triggers when one source contacts five or more distinct TCP destination ports within an incident. Confidence is labeled moderate and is a rule interpretation, not a probability. A scan does not prove intent, access, or compromise.<br><br>Findings cite the exact stored event IDs used by the rule.</div></section></div>`}
